276
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:46,970
Yes.

277
00:14:47,810 --> 00:14:48,930
Orange costume.

278
00:14:49,410 --> 00:14:52,090
And do not tell Jam about this, okay?

279
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:55,250
Though I look like this,
I'm a spirit with good morals.

280
00:14:55,490 --> 00:14:57,090
Once the money is in my bank account,

281
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,690
I'll keep my mouth shut.

282
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:01,770
Oh...

283
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,210
Oh, you.

284
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,310
Umm, here.

285
00:15:05,330 --> 00:15:06,530
[Incoming Transfer: 50,000 baht]

286
00:15:07,010 --> 00:15:08,170
Thank you, Sarm.

287
00:15:08,810 --> 00:15:10,490
I hope you get to rule the world.

288
00:15:26,390 --> 00:15:27,890
What? Sarm?!

289
00:15:28,050 --> 00:15:29,130
Where did he go?!

290
00:15:33,410 --> 00:15:34,450
Sarm!

291
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:36,250
Sarm!

292
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:57,530
Good evening, Mr. Sarm.
Are you interested in knocking some cans?

293
00:15:57,730 --> 00:15:58,490
Can you can a can?

294
00:15:59,770 --> 00:16:00,610
Just kidding.

295
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:02,290
What are the prizes?

296
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:04,490
The Charm Doll,
the Enchanted Doll, and the Spellbound Doll.

297
00:16:04,510 --> 00:16:06,430
I'll take all the balls
that you have.

298
00:16:06,450 --> 00:16:07,290
Sure.

299
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:08,310
Wait a minute.

300
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:09,290
I got here first.

301
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:10,810
Did you pay, though?

302
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:14,970
Just a kid in his twenties...?

303
00:16:15,530 --> 00:16:17,450
Will I be accused of bullying someone younger?

304
00:16:17,770 --> 00:16:18,410
Right.

305
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:20,690
It wouldn't be wise to use my power.

306
00:16:21,050 --> 00:16:22,130
We'll share half of the balls we get, then.

307
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:24,090
I'm good. Thank you.

308
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,520
Whatever suits you.

309
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:30,170
Can I have a ball, please?

310
00:16:30,850 --> 00:16:31,490
Here.

311
00:16:38,970 --> 00:16:40,250
Mr. Sarm.

312
00:16:40,650 --> 00:16:42,230
Which name should I engrave on the first doll?

313
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:43,350
- Engraving a name?
- A name.

314
00:16:43,370 --> 00:16:45,130
- Engraving a name?
- A name is important.

315
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:48,430
Is there a character limit?

316
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:49,630
- No.
- No limits either.

317
00:16:49,650 --> 00:16:50,330
Okay.

318
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:52,530
Alright, for the the Charm Doll,

319
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:58,450
let's do "Traiphop's Jiranat."

320
00:16:59,650 --> 00:17:00,870
How lovely.

321
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:01,930
Of course.

322
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:13,980
Mr. Sarm, and what about the Enchanted Doll?

323
00:17:13,990 --> 00:17:15,170
Oh, the Enchanted Doll, too.

324
00:17:16,329 --> 00:17:17,130
The Enchanted Doll.

325
00:17:17,329 --> 00:17:18,690
I went with our legal names...
Oh, nicknames.

326
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:23,410
Sarm belongs to Jam,
XOXO, kiss, kiss, then.

327
00:17:23,569 --> 00:17:24,690
Very sweet.

328
00:17:25,450 --> 00:17:26,569
Of course.

329
00:17:39,290 --> 00:17:41,010
Oh, anything else?

330
00:17:41,050 --> 00:17:42,450
- That's all.
- That's all?

331
00:17:42,610 --> 00:17:43,890
- We're doing this for real now.
- Right.

332
00:17:48,210 --> 00:17:49,730
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

333
00:17:55,930 --> 00:17:57,430
- Awesome!
- Well done, Mr. Sarm.

334
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:07,610
Jam.

335
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:09,690
There are blind boxes, too.

336
00:18:10,010 --> 00:18:11,290
There are ten boxes.

337
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:13,730
Which one would you choose?

338
00:18:14,090 --> 00:18:15,510
The third one.

339
00:18:15,530 --> 00:18:18,050
Oh, the third one...

340
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:20,050
Someone's madly in love.

341
00:18:32,010 --> 00:18:32,810
Okay.

342
00:18:35,010 --> 00:18:36,330
I got a devil horns headband.

343
00:18:40,430 --> 00:18:42,730
[Wasin: Come see me]

344
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:44,690
Jam,

345
00:18:45,490 --> 00:18:47,730
I need to go see...

346
00:18:49,610 --> 00:18:50,970
Wasin now.

347
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:53,670
Lantao...

348
00:18:53,690 --> 00:18:54,810
What really is going on?

349
00:18:54,830 --> 00:18:55,950
It's nothing.

350
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:57,150
Are you sure?

351
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:58,210
Yes.

352
00:18:58,450 --> 00:18:59,610
I'll see you in a bit.

353
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:00,780
Mm.

354
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:11,750
[Sarm: Where are you, my baby ghoul?]

355
00:19:11,770 --> 00:19:12,730
Sarm?

356
00:19:16,810 --> 00:19:17,730
Little Jam.

357
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:20,970
Little Jam.

358
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:22,210
What did you get?

359
00:19:22,450 --> 00:19:24,290
I just opened a blind box,

360
00:19:25,530 --> 00:19:26,890
and I got a devil horns headband.

361
00:19:27,930 --> 00:19:28,690
You don't like it?

362
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:31,570
I prefer shaman prayer beads more.

363
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:34,330
Okay, I'll buy you a prayer bead factory tomorrow.

364
00:19:34,890 --> 00:19:36,600
- That is crazy, Sarm.
- Huh?

365
00:19:37,550 --> 00:19:38,770
And what about you?

366
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:40,290
What did you get?

367
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:41,010
These.

368
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:43,170
I won a pair of dolls.

369
00:19:43,410 --> 00:19:44,810
They're the Charm Doll
and the Enchanted Doll.

370
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:46,650
What do you think?
Aren't they adorable?

371
00:19:48,150 --> 00:19:49,810
Come on, look at him. This way.

372
00:19:51,030 --> 00:19:52,030
I think...

373
00:19:52,050 --> 00:19:53,820
I do not think they go well together.

374
00:19:54,890 --> 00:19:55,930
Just like us.

375
00:19:56,930 --> 00:19:58,290
Still, we worked it out, didn't we?

376
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:02,690
Oh, hey.

377
00:20:03,390 --> 00:20:05,070
Remember the night we confessed our love?

378
00:20:06,150 --> 00:20:07,610
It is unforgettable.

379
00:20:09,090 --> 00:20:11,250
You were wearing a giant crab costume.

380
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:13,810
The theme of the party was related to ghosts,

381
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:16,810
yet you were the only one in a crab costume.

382
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:18,090
What?

383
00:20:18,810 --> 00:20:19,970
There are crab spirits, you know?

384
00:20:20,450 --> 00:20:21,410
Like pervert ghost.

385
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:23,730
Let me tell you something.

386
00:20:23,830 --> 00:20:25,330
This pervert ghost

387
00:20:25,630 --> 00:20:27,810
will haunt you

388
00:20:28,050 --> 00:20:29,410
forever.

389
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:31,810
- Boo!
- Hey, Sarm!

390
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:32,760
You scared me.

391
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:34,130
- Boo!
- Hey!

392
00:20:35,450 --> 00:20:37,150
- Help me!
- You want some of this?

393
00:20:37,170 --> 00:20:39,130
The pervert ghost is going to eat my liver!

394
00:20:41,090 --> 00:20:45,810
[Halloween with You]

395
00:21:03,450 --> 00:21:04,250
Why are you smiling?

396
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:07,050
Today was so fun.

397
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:09,850
When did you have the most fun?

398
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:13,810
When you got jealous.

399
00:21:18,010 --> 00:21:19,370
Huh, I wasn't jealous.

400
00:21:25,890 --> 00:21:27,370
Oh...

401
00:21:30,730 --> 00:21:34,090
You were searching for Toi-ting
throughout the whole event.

402
00:21:35,970 --> 00:21:37,330
Was that not being jealous?

403
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,120
I was

404
00:21:43,690 --> 00:21:45,490
providing close protection.

405
00:21:51,690 --> 00:21:52,730
Sarm.

406
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:53,970
Yes?

407
00:21:56,370 --> 00:21:58,630
What if someone flirted with you at the event?

408
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:01,100
Oh, that's impossible.

409
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:04,010
What if it happened?

410
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:08,410
I'd say that I already have a spouse.

411
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:11,210
And he's extremely adorable, too.

412
00:22:13,010 --> 00:22:13,810
And that...

413
00:22:15,010 --> 00:22:16,330
I really do love him.

414
00:22:18,130 --> 00:22:19,410
You have a good way with words.

415
00:22:21,650 --> 00:22:22,290
Hey.

416
00:22:22,770 --> 00:22:23,410
Hm?

417
00:22:25,210 --> 00:22:27,810
Can I give you a scrub bath tonight, my dear?

418
00:22:33,090 --> 00:22:33,970
Would that cost anything?

419
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:35,180
It's free for life.

420
00:22:36,070 --> 00:22:37,170
No strings attached.

421
00:23:07,890 --> 00:23:08,970
Shall we begin?

422
00:23:13,050 --> 00:23:14,170
Let's get it done and head to bed quickly.

423
00:23:16,130 --> 00:23:17,090
Why?

424
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:18,890
I have to wake up early tomorrow.

425
00:23:24,410 --> 00:23:26,490
How about we stay up the whole night, then?

426
00:23:41,410 --> 00:23:42,130
Oh.

427
00:23:51,090 --> 00:23:52,450
Are those my glasses?

428
00:24:07,490 --> 00:24:08,470
And...

429
00:24:09,690 --> 00:24:11,570
Where are they, then?

430
00:24:15,770 --> 00:24:17,130
Are they right here?

431
00:24:22,970 --> 00:24:23,930
Let's get it on, then.

432
00:24:31,090 --> 00:24:32,350
Your migraine pills?

433
00:24:32,370 --> 00:24:33,270
Always with me.

434
00:24:33,290 --> 00:24:34,270
Your shaving kit?

435
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:35,290
Already in the luggage.

436
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:36,790
Leg warmers?

437
00:24:36,810 --> 00:24:37,810
Sunglasses?

438
00:24:37,910 --> 00:24:38,750
Belts?

439
00:24:38,770 --> 00:24:39,610
Lotions?

440
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:42,290
My spouse has already taken care of them.

441
00:24:43,090 --> 00:24:44,970
I didn't forget anything, my dear.

442
00:24:45,130 --> 00:24:45,930
You did.

443
00:24:46,890 --> 00:24:47,690
What is it?

444
00:24:48,130 --> 00:24:48,690
Huh?

445
00:24:48,850 --> 00:24:50,450
You forgot to kiss me.

446
00:24:55,590 --> 00:24:56,410
Ow...

447
00:24:58,450 --> 00:24:59,170
Hey.

448
00:24:59,850 --> 00:25:00,670
While I'm away,

449
00:25:00,690 --> 00:25:02,530
do not wander off on your own, okay?

450
00:25:03,650 --> 00:25:05,450
I will not wander off on my own.

451
00:25:08,050 --> 00:25:09,810
I will go with Lantao.

452
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:11,250
No.

453
00:25:13,090 --> 00:25:13,770
Don't do that.

454
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:16,380
Don't forget to eat, too.

455
00:25:17,210 --> 00:25:18,590
I've already told Mod-dang

456
00:25:18,610 --> 00:25:20,130
to prepare food for you.

457
00:25:20,370 --> 00:25:22,250
Every meal, every day.

458
00:25:22,410 --> 00:25:23,730
That is too much, Sarm.

459
00:25:24,150 --> 00:25:26,130
Hey, if nobody prepares food for you,

460
00:25:26,670 --> 00:25:28,290
you'll sneak out to have junk food.

461
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:29,750
Mm...

462
00:25:30,250 --> 00:25:31,810
I will stay fed. Don't worry.

463
00:25:32,850 --> 00:25:33,890
On top of that,

464
00:25:35,150 --> 00:25:37,130
don't overwork yourself.

465
00:25:37,310 --> 00:25:39,870
If I catch you doing it again,

466
00:25:39,890 --> 00:25:40,570
we'll see about that!

467
00:25:42,450 --> 00:25:43,370
Understood?

468
00:25:46,570 --> 00:25:47,730
What will you do to me?

469
00:25:48,410 --> 00:25:49,090
Hm?

470
00:25:49,610 --> 00:25:50,410
I will...

471
00:25:53,890 --> 00:25:55,550
ask you to take it easy.

472
00:25:55,570 --> 00:25:56,690
All you do is work.

473
00:25:57,490 --> 00:25:58,290
I'm worried about you.

474
00:25:59,710 --> 00:26:00,610
Understood?

475
00:26:02,010 --> 00:26:03,370
One last thing.

476
00:26:04,170 --> 00:26:05,090
Don't...

477
00:26:05,410 --> 00:26:06,770
forget to miss me.

478
00:26:09,930 --> 00:26:11,250
Same to you, Sarm.

479
00:26:12,210 --> 00:26:13,810
Eat well, okay?

480
00:26:14,570 --> 00:26:15,370
Absolutely.

481
00:26:17,090 --> 00:26:18,290
Should I get you some treats from there?

482
00:26:18,810 --> 00:26:20,250
I am not a kid.

483
00:26:20,770 --> 00:26:21,510
Hey.

484
00:26:22,690 --> 00:26:23,890
I'll be away only for two weeks.

485
00:26:24,290 --> 00:26:25,250
I'll be back in a flash.

486
00:26:28,450 --> 00:26:29,810
Take good care of Little Jam, okay?

487
00:26:29,890 --> 00:26:31,030
If something happens to him,

488
00:26:31,050 --> 00:26:32,130
I won't let it slide.

489
00:26:32,370 --> 00:26:33,410
- Yes, Boss.
- Huh.

490
00:26:33,610 --> 00:26:34,850
I can lose anything,

491
00:26:35,570 --> 00:26:36,610
but not you, Little Jam,

492
00:26:36,690 --> 00:26:37,850
I can't lose you.

493
00:26:38,390 --> 00:26:40,570
No thief is coming to steal me.

494
00:26:40,610 --> 00:26:42,370
Well, I care about what's mine.

495
00:26:43,930 --> 00:26:44,850
I'll be going now.

496
00:26:48,370 --> 00:26:49,170
Bye-bye.

497
00:26:49,970 --> 00:26:51,130
Bye-bye.

498
00:26:54,010 --> 00:26:54,810
See you.

499
00:26:55,090 --> 00:26:55,890
Bye-bye.

500
00:26:57,090 --> 00:26:58,090
Bye-bye.

501
00:26:59,070 --> 00:27:00,490
Take care of yourself.

502
00:27:10,570 --> 00:27:11,490
Bye-bye.

503
00:27:20,470 --> 00:27:21,210
Wait!

504
00:27:21,930 --> 00:27:22,690
I'm right here.

505
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:25,290
What?

506
00:27:25,650 --> 00:27:26,490
Huh?

507
00:27:27,250 --> 00:27:28,290
Sarm?!

508
00:27:29,250 --> 00:27:30,750
Why did you not hop on the car?

509
00:27:30,770 --> 00:27:31,930
It left before I could.

510
00:27:32,090 --> 00:27:32,990
I'll be seeing you.

511
00:27:33,210 --> 00:27:34,450
Bye-bye, Little Jam.

512
00:27:34,830 --> 00:27:35,690
Miss you.

513
00:27:36,110 --> 00:27:37,930
- Bye-bye.
- Don't forget to miss me, too!

514
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:39,230
Bye-bye.

515
00:27:39,250 --> 00:27:40,450
Bye-bye.

516
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:41,930
Hey, back up the car right now.

517
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:43,290
Should I fire you?

518
00:27:44,810 --> 00:27:47,650
[One week later]

519
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:57,370
Simply follow the plans
that have been laid out.

520
00:27:58,390 --> 00:27:59,390
Thank you very much.

521
00:27:59,690 --> 00:28:01,030
[Sarm: Miss you, babe]

522
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:05,360
[Sarm: I need your love.
I don't have the energy to work]

523
00:28:10,610 --> 00:28:11,970
Okay.

524
00:28:12,670 --> 00:28:14,750
Thank you.
[Sarm: Has your work been draining?]

525
00:28:14,770 --> 00:28:17,910
[Sarm: Don't forget to eat]

526
00:28:17,930 --> 00:28:19,790
[Day 8]

527
00:28:19,810 --> 00:28:21,770
Would you like to have any menu in particular?

528
00:28:22,370 --> 00:28:24,450
Anything will do, Dad.

529
00:28:25,670 --> 00:28:26,490
Nim,

530
00:28:26,500 --> 00:28:28,410
- Yes?
- serve him a dish of anything.

531
00:28:28,610 --> 00:28:30,430
Understood. I'll get it ready soon.

532
00:28:30,450 --> 00:28:31,240
Mm, wait.

533
00:28:31,260 --> 00:28:32,050
You know what to get?

534
00:28:33,850 --> 00:28:36,050
- I'll have a look in the kitchen.
- Okay.

535
00:28:37,810 --> 00:28:40,090
How are you? How is your work here?

536
00:28:40,370 --> 00:28:41,450
It has been great,

537
00:28:41,850 --> 00:28:43,810
I am still settling in.

538
00:28:45,650 --> 00:28:47,890
Okay. Here, let's settle in.

539
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:52,090
Welcome.

540
00:28:52,490 --> 00:28:53,870
Thank you.

541
00:28:58,250 --> 00:28:59,510
[Day 11]

542
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:01,130
Jam, can you help me with this?

543
00:29:01,410 --> 00:29:03,150
I'm thinking of buying this collection of clothes,

544
00:29:03,170 --> 00:29:04,670
and I trust your sense of fashion.

545
00:29:04,690 --> 00:29:07,130
Can you pick the one you like?

546
00:29:08,110 --> 00:29:09,410
Whoa.

547
00:29:10,410 --> 00:29:11,930
I think these are all beautiful.

548
00:29:12,330 --> 00:29:14,250
Mm, this crop top looks...

549
00:29:14,570 --> 00:29:15,530
interesting.

550
00:29:15,770 --> 00:29:16,730
What do you think?

551
00:29:17,150 --> 00:29:17,890
Is it a wonderful pick?

552
00:29:18,810 --> 00:29:19,970
I think it is.

553
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:23,530
I have never seen you

554
00:29:23,850 --> 00:29:25,850
in an outfit this sexy before.

555
00:29:26,530 --> 00:29:28,310
I never have the guts to wear one.

556
00:29:28,330 --> 00:29:30,390
You would look fantastic in any of these.

557
00:29:30,410 --> 00:29:32,170
Oh, are you telling a white lie?

558
00:29:32,470 --> 00:29:34,390
I am not. Well...

559
00:29:34,810 --> 00:29:37,110
Just look at your body and everything.

560
00:29:37,130 --> 00:29:38,990
- Nonsense...
- They all look good.

561
00:29:39,010 --> 00:29:40,290
You're flattering me, Jam.

562
00:29:40,750 --> 00:29:42,910
How about we wear matching outfits instead?

563
00:29:44,090 --> 00:29:45,550
I'm going to wear the crop top,

564
00:29:45,570 --> 00:29:46,890
and you might wear

565
00:29:46,950 --> 00:29:49,030
some cute cardigan.

566
00:29:49,050 --> 00:29:50,330
But both with the same pattern.

567
00:29:50,690 --> 00:29:52,790
- Mm.
- Right? It's a lovely idea, isn't it?

568
00:29:53,410 --> 00:29:54,990
Then we might also...

569
00:29:55,010 --> 00:29:57,250
take some photos and show them to Sarm.

570
00:29:59,770 --> 00:30:01,250
I think it is a good idea.

571
00:30:03,250 --> 00:30:05,250
I believe this one really suits you.

572
00:30:12,970 --> 00:30:14,730
This one also looks interesting.

573
00:30:20,330 --> 00:30:21,250
Jam.

574
00:30:22,390 --> 00:30:23,330
Jam.

575
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:25,810
- Jam!
- Yes?

576
00:30:27,350 --> 00:30:28,770
You miss him, don't you?

577
00:30:31,570 --> 00:30:32,970
Who are you referring to, Song?

578
00:30:33,030 --> 00:30:33,670
There.

579
00:30:34,530 --> 00:30:35,970
I can see right through you.

580
00:30:36,410 --> 00:30:38,330
Who am I missing? No...no one.

581
00:30:38,350 --> 00:30:40,630
- Song.
- Stop pretending, Jam.

582
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:41,690
The eyes

583
00:30:41,890 --> 00:30:43,410
never lie.

584
00:30:45,110 --> 00:30:46,770
I am closing my eyes, then.

585
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:50,410
So you are flustered.
Are you admitting to that?

586
00:30:51,170 --> 00:30:52,290
Ow...

587
00:30:52,430 --> 00:30:54,510
Stop teasing me, Song.

588
00:30:54,530 --> 00:30:56,650
I get it. You two are far apart.

589
00:30:57,690 --> 00:30:59,730
It's normal to miss your partner.

590
00:31:01,790 --> 00:31:03,070
There. You're blushing again.

591
00:31:04,290 --> 00:31:05,790
Aw, you're blushing so much.

592
00:31:05,810 --> 00:31:07,690
Even your ears are now red, too.

593
00:31:08,170 --> 00:31:09,550
You miss him that much, don't you?

594
00:31:09,570 --> 00:31:11,090
Come on, Song.

595
00:31:11,490 --> 00:31:12,890
- Oh, your cheeks are red.
- Oh.

596
00:31:12,930 --> 00:31:14,330
I will tease you back.

597
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:17,550
Once you have a partner,

598
00:31:17,570 --> 00:31:19,130
I will tease you every day.

599
00:31:19,290 --> 00:31:20,490
Go ahead, then.

600
00:31:21,490 --> 00:31:22,650
[Day 13]

601
00:31:22,670 --> 00:31:23,950
[Sarm: What are you doing?]

602
00:31:23,970 --> 00:31:25,390
[Sarm: Miss you, babe]

603
00:31:25,410 --> 00:31:26,680
[Jam: Do you?]

604
00:31:27,370 --> 00:31:28,530
I cannot wait.

605
00:31:57,570 --> 00:31:58,530
Sarm!

606
00:31:59,290 --> 00:31:59,930
Babe.

607
00:32:00,370 --> 00:32:01,330
I'm home.

608
00:32:06,970 --> 00:32:08,050
I missed you so much.

609
00:32:14,730 --> 00:32:15,890
Are you tired?

610
00:32:21,970 --> 00:32:23,490
There.

611
00:32:34,850 --> 00:32:35,970
It's been too long.

612
00:32:40,070 --> 00:32:41,730
You were away for two weeks.

613
00:32:44,210 --> 00:32:45,370
Are you tired?

614
00:32:46,650 --> 00:32:47,650
Are you?

615
00:32:50,290 --> 00:32:51,450
I missed you more than anything.

616
00:32:53,230 --> 00:32:54,330
These past two weeks,

617
00:32:54,790 --> 00:32:55,970
I'd been missing you a lot.

618
00:32:57,010 --> 00:32:57,850
I missed you so much.

619
00:32:58,270 --> 00:32:59,130
I really did.

620
00:33:00,170 --> 00:33:00,890
So very much.

621
00:33:34,650 --> 00:33:36,890
I missed you a lot, too.

622
00:33:46,130 --> 00:33:47,170
How much do you miss me,

623
00:33:52,850 --> 00:33:54,290
- huh?
- Very much.

624
00:33:56,570 --> 00:33:57,770
This much.

625
00:33:59,930 --> 00:34:01,010
I missed this

626
00:34:02,450 --> 00:34:03,370
and this.

627
00:34:04,850 --> 00:34:05,710
And this.

628
00:34:05,730 --> 00:34:06,530
This, too.

629
00:34:07,110 --> 00:34:08,050
- Also this.
- Ow.

630
00:34:08,250 --> 00:34:08,949
This, too.

631
00:34:08,969 --> 00:34:10,170
Ow.

632
00:34:21,690 --> 00:34:22,889
I missed this voice.

633
00:34:23,170 --> 00:34:24,330
I missed everything.

634
00:34:53,290 --> 00:34:54,570
If that is the case,

635
00:34:56,630 --> 00:35:00,130
go ahead and knock yourself out tonight.

636
00:35:04,730 --> 00:35:05,570
Don't mind if I do.

637
00:35:24,310 --> 00:35:26,610
Please do not be away for this long again.

638
00:35:30,010 --> 00:35:31,010
If I could choose,

639
00:35:31,490 --> 00:35:32,530
I'd never want to go anywhere.

640
00:35:33,050 --> 00:35:34,410
I'd never want to be away from you.

641
00:35:41,350 --> 00:35:42,730
What about the meetings?

642
00:35:43,330 --> 00:35:44,530
Online meetings exist,

643
00:35:46,570 --> 00:35:47,530
right?

644
00:35:55,610 --> 00:35:58,290
I really missed you, you know?

645
00:36:01,330 --> 00:36:02,490
So did I.

646
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:05,370
No matter how far apart we are,

647
00:36:05,930 --> 00:36:08,410
my house is always right here.

648
00:36:08,890 --> 00:36:09,730
Right here.

649
00:36:10,010 --> 00:36:10,810
And here.

650
00:36:11,170 --> 00:36:12,090
Here, too.

651
00:36:42,890 --> 00:36:43,810
Are you hungry?

652
00:36:44,810 --> 00:36:46,490
I am still full, actually.

653
00:36:46,630 --> 00:36:47,730
Tell me if you're hungry, then.

654
00:36:48,690 --> 00:36:51,450
You will take me to a restaurant, right?

655
00:36:51,650 --> 00:36:52,570
No.

656
00:36:53,330 --> 00:36:54,450
I'll stop the car,

657
00:36:54,610 --> 00:36:56,850
and you'll have to jump into the water

658
00:36:57,070 --> 00:36:58,010
and catch some fish yourself.

659
00:36:59,770 --> 00:37:01,790
You are messing with me again, Sarm.

660
00:37:01,810 --> 00:37:02,850
Just kidding.

661
00:37:03,130 --> 00:37:05,150
I made you sandwiches.

662
00:37:05,170 --> 00:37:06,650
And I got you pomegranate juice.

663
00:37:07,610 --> 00:37:08,850
They're in the back.

664
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:13,730
How lovely.

665
00:37:14,950 --> 00:37:16,570
Then love me a whole bunch.

666
00:37:18,410 --> 00:37:19,930
I already do.

667
00:37:20,730 --> 00:37:21,850
You love me a lot,

668
00:37:22,370 --> 00:37:24,010
then you have to spoil me a bunch, too.

669
00:37:27,530 --> 00:37:29,690
You are being clingy.

670
00:37:29,930 --> 00:37:31,310
You have something in mind, do you not?

671
00:37:31,330 --> 00:37:32,250
You caught me.

672
00:37:32,850 --> 00:37:33,810
Well...

673
00:37:36,770 --> 00:37:37,850
Do you know that

674
00:37:39,330 --> 00:37:40,490
a good spouse

675
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:42,850
is the one...

676
00:37:43,370 --> 00:37:45,490
who wears a fluffy tail?

677
00:37:46,790 --> 00:37:47,930
A lovely

678
00:37:47,950 --> 00:37:48,930
and fluffy tail.

679
00:37:52,610 --> 00:37:54,610
And do you know this?

680
00:37:55,130 --> 00:37:55,730
Yes?

681
00:37:55,910 --> 00:37:58,090
Do you know that a good spouse for me...

682
00:37:58,390 --> 00:37:59,200
What is it?

683
00:37:59,470 --> 00:38:00,690
is a new spouse entirely?

684
00:38:02,450 --> 00:38:04,570
Oh, Little Jam.

685
00:38:05,650 --> 00:38:06,850
I was joking.

686
00:38:08,420 --> 00:38:09,750
I just want to entertain my spouse.

687
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:10,940
So that tonight

688
00:38:14,100 --> 00:38:15,740
you'll have to entertain me in return.

689
00:38:16,700 --> 00:38:18,140
Sarm.

690
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:21,620
Oh, you slapped me, too?

691
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:26,040
You always find ways to come back to that topic.

692
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:29,180
Just want to be clingy with you...

693
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:30,820
Let us hit the road.

694
00:38:30,860 --> 00:38:32,780
- Find.
- Are you heading out or not?

695
00:38:32,860 --> 00:38:34,620
Sure, let's head out.

696
00:39:01,530 --> 00:39:02,690
Sarm...

697
00:39:32,790 --> 00:39:33,840
Sarm?

698
00:39:38,670 --> 00:39:40,090
Oh, Sarm.

699
00:39:40,110 --> 00:39:41,390
Ta-da!

700
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:43,490
I bought a bunch of crabs for you.

701
00:39:43,510 --> 00:39:44,190
Look, look.

702
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:51,890
You were sleeping,

703
00:39:51,910 --> 00:39:52,910
so I didn't want to wake you up.

704
00:39:52,930 --> 00:39:53,790
Feeling hungry?

705
00:40:00,870 --> 00:40:02,770
I want to go for a stroll.

706
00:40:02,790 --> 00:40:03,870
Then, let's go.

707
00:40:04,090 --> 00:40:04,710
Come on.

708
00:40:05,230 --> 00:40:05,830
Alright.

709
00:40:08,230 --> 00:40:08,950
Let us go.

710
00:40:25,130 --> 00:40:26,750
Sarm, do you remember that

711
00:40:28,390 --> 00:40:31,670
you climbed up a coconut tree
because some kids dared you to?

712
00:40:32,590 --> 00:40:34,230
Who would forget their own achievements?

713
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:42,110
You gave me a lot of headaches back then.

714
00:40:45,070 --> 00:40:45,670
But...

715
00:40:46,390 --> 00:40:47,550
If it wasn't for that day,

716
00:40:48,910 --> 00:40:50,210
we wouldn't end up together like this.

717
00:40:55,650 --> 00:40:56,590
For many things that have happened,

718
00:40:58,230 --> 00:40:59,630
after looking back at them,

719
00:41:01,290 --> 00:41:03,290
there's a lot that I'm grateful for.

720
00:41:06,790 --> 00:41:07,950
I want to thank you

721
00:41:08,670 --> 00:41:09,950
for helping me to be here.

722
00:41:17,630 --> 00:41:19,030
Because you're more than just love.

723
00:41:22,510 --> 00:41:23,870
You're the other half of me.

724
00:41:27,710 --> 00:41:28,710
You're my other half,

725
00:41:30,830 --> 00:41:31,750
my thinking partner,

726
00:41:34,790 --> 00:41:36,070
and my support.

727
00:41:43,090 --> 00:41:44,230
I love you, Little Jam.

728
00:41:46,790 --> 00:41:47,750
I really do.

729
00:41:55,110 --> 00:41:57,070
I love you, too, Sarm.

730
00:42:00,150 --> 00:42:01,550
I love you more than anyone else.

731
00:42:03,110 --> 00:42:04,350
When do you love me the most?

732
00:42:08,350 --> 00:42:10,960
When you're aware of your own surroundings.

733
00:42:13,110 --> 00:42:14,640
That almost ended on a positive note.

734
00:42:25,950 --> 00:42:27,390
I never thought that

735
00:42:28,070 --> 00:42:30,630
someone who I fought to the death with

736
00:42:35,190 --> 00:42:37,030
would become my soulmate.

737
00:42:41,390 --> 00:42:43,110
Now and forever,

738
00:42:46,590 --> 00:42:48,710
I want you to be a part of my life.

739
00:42:54,010 --> 00:42:56,180
The one who can be at my side

740
00:42:57,490 --> 00:42:58,790
can be no one else

741
00:42:59,790 --> 00:43:00,710
but you...

742
00:43:02,270 --> 00:43:03,190
Jiranat.

743
00:43:26,970 --> 00:43:27,470
Oh.

744
00:43:28,070 --> 00:43:28,990
Little Jam.

745
00:43:29,230 --> 00:43:30,870
- Yes?
- No, come here.

746
00:43:31,310 --> 00:43:32,990
This is very wrong.

747
00:43:34,390 --> 00:43:35,070
Here.

748
00:43:41,590 --> 00:43:44,360
You're adorable, so you can have another bite.

749
00:43:45,230 --> 00:43:47,350
Oh, it's on your lips.

750
00:43:56,190 --> 00:43:57,190
All clean now.

751
00:43:58,840 --> 00:44:00,920
- You take care of me so well.
- Of course.

752
00:44:02,710 --> 00:44:04,430
We have finally made it back home, have we not?

753
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:06,950
Yeah.

754
00:44:07,190 --> 00:44:07,830
But

755
00:44:08,430 --> 00:44:10,350
I don't know why I can still
smell the sea.

756
00:44:11,790 --> 00:44:13,750
You are always being so extra.

757
00:44:17,050 --> 00:44:18,270
So extra.

758
00:44:18,870 --> 00:44:19,950
Eat up.

759
00:44:20,150 --> 00:44:21,470
Or else you'll miss

760
00:44:21,700 --> 00:44:23,560
these tasty treats when you're back to work.

761
00:44:28,630 --> 00:44:29,950
I think...

762
00:44:30,340 --> 00:44:32,760
I miss the one who cooks for me more.

763
00:44:33,810 --> 00:44:34,910
You mean the chef?

764
00:44:40,200 --> 00:44:41,240
- Yes.
- Oh.

765
00:44:42,630 --> 00:44:43,590
Lucky you,

766
00:44:44,470 --> 00:44:45,510
because that handsome chef

767
00:44:46,390 --> 00:44:47,520
is your spouse.

768
00:44:50,230 --> 00:44:51,570
You are so full of yourself.

769
00:44:51,590 --> 00:44:52,350
Always.

770
00:44:57,930 --> 00:44:59,350
Back to eating.

771
00:45:00,470 --> 00:45:01,670
Let me feed you, too.

772
00:45:03,100 --> 00:45:04,610
Alright...

773
00:45:04,970 --> 00:45:06,430
Sarm, open wide.

774
00:45:11,710 --> 00:45:12,630
Is it sweet?

775
00:45:13,950 --> 00:45:14,790
It is,

776
00:45:15,490 --> 00:45:16,670
but not as sweet as your lips.

777
00:45:21,740 --> 00:45:22,980
It is a shame that

778
00:45:23,550 --> 00:45:25,070
the trip is over.

779
00:45:26,110 --> 00:45:26,830
Hey,

780
00:45:27,750 --> 00:45:29,390
our story isn't over, though.

781
00:45:30,150 --> 00:45:30,790
Mm.

782
00:45:32,120 --> 00:45:33,500
I have to wake up early

783
00:45:35,110 --> 00:45:36,150
to go to work

784
00:45:36,850 --> 00:45:37,710
and go to meetings.

785
00:45:39,150 --> 00:45:40,150
It's as exhausting as always.

786
00:45:42,030 --> 00:45:44,230
But you will get to come home
and have dinner with me.

787
00:45:46,030 --> 00:45:47,470
And fight over a blanket.

788
00:45:48,290 --> 00:45:49,640
You stole my blanket.

789
00:45:49,770 --> 00:45:50,840
That's incorrect.

790
00:45:50,860 --> 00:45:51,610
Am I wrong?

791
00:45:54,110 --> 00:45:55,550
I just wanted to hug you.

792
00:46:16,730 --> 00:46:18,510
Thank you, Sarm.

793
00:46:20,870 --> 00:46:22,030
For what?

794
00:46:25,270 --> 00:46:27,990
For turning ordinary days

795
00:46:30,290 --> 00:46:31,950
into memorable ones.

796
00:46:45,030 --> 00:46:45,670
Hey.

797
00:46:48,070 --> 00:46:49,310
Promise me one thing.

798
00:46:52,830 --> 00:46:53,910
What is it?

799
00:46:56,830 --> 00:46:57,830
No matter how sad,

800
00:46:59,750 --> 00:47:00,550
how happy,

801
00:47:03,510 --> 00:47:04,550
how upset,

802
00:47:06,070 --> 00:47:07,750
how tired you are or how much you cry,

803
00:47:11,290 --> 00:47:12,950
you have to come home
and have dinner with me.

804
00:47:17,670 --> 00:47:18,830
I promise you,

805
00:47:20,470 --> 00:47:21,790
my spouse.

806
00:47:25,470 --> 00:47:26,350
You're the best.

807
00:47:29,230 --> 00:47:30,310
Back then,

808
00:47:30,950 --> 00:47:32,670
I once believed that love

809
00:47:33,070 --> 00:47:35,270
meant searching for the perfect person,

810
00:47:35,410 --> 00:47:37,410
but only through living my own life

811
00:47:38,990 --> 00:47:40,590
have I realized that...

812
00:47:40,910 --> 00:47:44,230
love means being
with someone who accepts our flaws

813
00:47:44,830 --> 00:47:47,110
and chooses to hold our hand every single day.

814
00:47:48,890 --> 00:47:50,550
I'm not the most talented man in the world.

815
00:47:51,210 --> 00:47:52,750
My words aren't always sweet.

816
00:47:53,190 --> 00:47:54,550
And I often make mistakes.

817
00:47:55,990 --> 00:47:57,590
But whenever I turn around,

818
00:47:57,910 --> 00:47:59,150
I'm always happy to see that

819
00:47:59,570 --> 00:48:01,230
the person next to me is still Jam.

820
00:48:02,210 --> 00:48:04,210
We have been through the days we fought,

821
00:48:07,860 --> 00:48:09,440
the days we longed for one another,

822
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:11,280
and the days we had to be apart.

823
00:48:13,320 --> 00:48:14,920
We pushed through and persevered.

824
00:48:15,670 --> 00:48:17,270
Because we never let go of each other's hands.

825
00:48:18,390 --> 00:48:21,590
What is the best part of my life?

826
00:48:27,510 --> 00:48:29,130
My answer would be...

827
00:48:29,710 --> 00:48:31,870
- the days I have you by my side.
- The days I have you by my side.

828
00:48:32,870 --> 00:48:35,430
The story of Traiphop and Jiranat

829
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,800
may have ended here,

830
00:48:38,950 --> 00:48:40,630
but our love story

831
00:48:40,950 --> 00:48:42,070
has only just begun.

832
00:48:49,220 --> 00:48:51,510
♫My mind keeps running wild♫

833
00:48:51,530 --> 00:48:53,470
♫Don't make me feel things, things♫

834
00:48:53,500 --> 00:48:55,960
♫The way you get close to me, me♫

835
00:48:55,980 --> 00:48:59,520
♫Can you just tell me how you feel?♫

836
00:48:59,550 --> 00:49:01,790
♫Do you feel this love is real?♫

837
00:49:01,810 --> 00:49:03,570
♫That kiss, kiss♫

838
00:49:03,590 --> 00:49:06,780
♫Was it a coincidence or destiny?♫

839
00:49:06,800 --> 00:49:07,960
♫Was that a genuine kiss,♫

840
00:49:07,970 --> 00:49:11,090
♫Or was it a one-time thing?♫

841
00:49:11,600 --> 00:49:13,640
♫Don't make me feel things, things♫

842
00:49:13,660 --> 00:49:16,200
♫The way you get close to me, me♫

843
00:49:16,210 --> 00:49:19,710
♫Can you just tell me how you feel?♫

844
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:21,990
♫Do you feel this love is real?♫

845
00:49:22,010 --> 00:49:23,800
♫That kiss, kiss♫

